States: Standards

Purpose:
  Defines standard states for .sdd entities.
  This is the single source of truth for all state definitions.

TaskStates:
  NEW:
    Description: Task has been created but not yet analyzed
  ANALYZING:
    Description: Task is being analyzed (scope, dependencies, risk)
  PLANNED:
    Description: Analysis complete, plan exists, ready for implementation
  READY:
    Description: All prerequisites met, waiting for execution slot
  IN_PROGRESS:
    Description: Work is actively being performed
  BLOCKED:
    Description: Work cannot continue due to an unresolved blocker
  REVIEW:
    Description: Work is under review
  TESTING:
    Description: Work is being tested (QA stage)
  SECURITY:
    Description: Work is under security validation (SC stage)
  VERIFYING:
    Description: Work is under final verification (VR stage)
  DONE:
    Description: Work is complete and verified
  FAILED:
    Description: Work has failed and requires recovery
  CANCELLED:
    Description: Work has been cancelled, will not proceed

EntityStates:
  DRAFT:
    Description: Initial creation, not ready
  EXPERIMENTAL:
    Description: Being tested, may change
  STABLE:
    Description: Production-ready, stable
  DEPRECATED:
    Description: Being phased out
  RETIRED:
    Description: No longer used

WorkflowStates:
  PENDING:
    Not started
  RUNNING:
    In progress
  PASSED:
    Completed successfully
  FAILED:
    Failed
  BLOCKED:
    Waiting for dependency
  SKIPPED:
    Not applicable
  WAIVED:
    Approved to skip
  EXPIRED:
    Waiver expired

GateStates:
  PENDING
  RUNNING
  PASSED
  FAILED
  BLOCKED
  SKIPPED
  WAIVED
  EXPIRED

CompactSymbols:
  Purpose: Inline state notation for .sdd files
  Symbols:
    +: done
    ~: active
    -: failed
    !: blocked
    ?: decision required
    >: next
    @: reference
    #: task
    =: created
    :: analyzing
    *: review
    ^: superseded
    _: archived
    x: cancelled
    [!]: attention required
    [x]: completed
    [ ]: pending

StateRules:
  [SS1]  All entities MUST have a state.
  [SS2]  State transitions MUST follow defined flows.
  [SS3]  ARCHIVED state preserves history, does not delete.
  [SS4]  WAIVED state requires expiration date.
  [SS5]  Compact symbols are for inline notation only — full state names are canonical.
  [SS6]  Task state machine is defined in workflow/state.sdd — do not duplicate here.

State: +
  